<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Homer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Homer is the ancient Greek poet to whom the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> are attributed, epic poems probably composed in the 8th or 7th century BCE from a long oral tradition. The Iliad tells of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trojan-war">Trojan War</a> and the Odyssey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseus">Odysseus</a>'s return home. Nothing certain is known of his life, but his poems were the foundation of Greek education and literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/homer.jpg" alt="Homer" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph by Mike Peel (www.mikepeel.net). · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Homer_At_the_British_Museum_2024_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
